# Tawks - Daily games, football and guests

![Football picks as a guest](/posts/tawks/010.webp)

## The word game

Sunday night I added a daily secret word game, like Contexto. You guess a word and it ranks how close you are using embeddings. 17,329 words in the vocabulary, 3,526 possible secrets.

Monday morning I swapped the hints for clue words that get warmer as you go, cut 1,638 of the secrets and tuned the scoring around ten guesses.

About half an hour later I replaced the whole game with a Connections style puzzle. Four groups of four, from a bank of 30 I wrote by hand.

```json
{"level": 4, "name": "Sound like numbers", "words": ["WON", "ATE", "FOR", "TOO"]}
```

So the first one lasted about twelve hours. That afternoon the bank got easier and you get one hint after two mistakes.

## Football

The Football hub has weekly pick'em and a season long survivor pool. It runs off ESPN's public scoreboard. Weeks go Wednesday to Wednesday, picks lock at kickoff and you get up to three locks a week. Later that day I added a fantasy lineup, QB, RB, WR and a flex, half PPR off the box scores.

ESPN stopped accepting date ranges on the scoreboard, so it fetches one day at a time now.

Button inputs stay in the workflow's responses. Tapping a lineup slot reused the game you picked for the last slot and jumped straight to its players.

It was all one channel at first. Now Picks, Lineup, Survivor, Leaderboard and Me are separate channels, each its own workflow, all one bot.

## Guests

You don't need an account anymore. Every visitor gets a guest session. You can look around public hubs and play the games, and there's a sign in prompt where the chat box would be. The API refuses writes from a guest. If you sign up the guest gets converted, so your game history stays yours.

Guests were all called "Guest" at first. Now you get something like GoldenSparrow-918.

The games were skipping a guest's saved state too, so a group you already solved stayed on the board and your picks looked blank. Also a dead guest token used to fail every call. Now it gets replaced.
